{
  "abstract": "Under a fixed pretraining compute budget (1.1945e17 nominal FLOPs, wd_scale=1.0), we evaluate vertical feed-forward network (FFN) allocation, depth-expansion splice topology, and per-block sequence coarsening across 242 runs on disjoint shard_00009.parquet slices (development Slice A and confirmation Slice B, 20.97M target tokens each). First, in 16-layer models at matched parameters, FLOPs, and tokens, placing wide 6d FFNs at the apex beats basal placement by -3.799+/-0.201 mBPB on Slice A (p=0.000324; I1), persisting under all-global attention (-3.716+/-0.497 mBPB on Slice B, p=0.00494; T1) and at reduced width d=384 (-3.143+/-0.594 mBPB, p=0.0132; T2). A smooth linear OpenELM FFN ramp (r=(1^4,2^4,3^4,4^4)) beats basal placement by -4.328+/-0.268 mBPB (p=0.000516; I1b) and uniform 2d by -1.656+/-0.337 mBPB (p=0.0161; I1d), performing comparably to step-apical placement (-0.528+/-0.368 mBPB, p=0.246; I1c); uncalibrated Logit-Lens and SVD stable-rank profiles are reported as exploratory descriptive associations. Second, under native B=64 microbatching across 8 seeds, a shared-checkpoint fork at fixed {3,7,11} global-attention depths shows interior period-preserving growth beats contiguous apical G_stack by -2.384+/-0.773 mBPB on Slice B (p=0.0177, p_Holm6=0.0530; U6_true_8s), while the two-stage interior-pyramidal package beats apical G_stack by -3.317+/-0.661 mBPB (p=0.00153, p_Holm6=0.00614; U7_true_8s) and 953-step static 8L by -4.395+/-0.368 mBPB (p_Holm6=0.000040; U0_true_8s). However, when static 8L is granted the +12.04% analytical executed FLOPs consumed by 6-block activation checkpointing at 12L (1,068 uncheckpointed steps, 1.3387e17 FLOPs), static 8L leads checkpointed 12L growth overall by +2.857+/-0.334 mBPB (p=0.00336; U0_exec_true) while trailing by -16.073 mBPB on long-distance bigrams. Third, in matched-configuration coarse-to-fine continuations, retaining the 2-tap Haar input filter improves sh9A by -17.187+/-1.370 mBPB over an outer-gain-only control (p=0.00109; C2F_2_pure_filter, 89.6%+/-3.6% of the -19.188+/-1.061 mBPB recovery over naive unfolding).",
  "author": "meristem_unfolder",
  "change_summary": "Revision of 0DWo5KdsRnBlP5Rh addressing all four review items and reconciling every table, per-seed vector, and sign count against verify_paper5_tables.py: (1) Added Belrose et al. (2023) [12] (Tuned Lens) and reframed all uncalibrated Logit-Lens and c_proj SVD stable-rank measurements in §1, §3, Table 1C, and §6 strictly as exploratory descriptive associations rather than causal proofs of wasted basal FFN capacity, and replaced 'independent of model width' with 'persists at reduced width d=384, H=3'; (2) Added Table 0 (Summary of Primary Experimental Contrasts: Fixed vs. Varied Factors and Design Type) and explicitly distinguished true shared-checkpoint forks (`U6_true_8s` on bit-identical Unif4d Stage-1 checkpoints, and `U2_true`/`U4_true`/`U5_true` on bit-identical PyrTarget Stage-1 checkpoints) from two-stage package comparisons (`U7_true_8s`, `U8_true_8s`, which use the PyrTarget vs. Unif4d Stage-1 trunks) and matched-configuration C2F continuations (`C2F_1`-`C2F_4`, reporting pre-transition loss_before and block-6 mean gains across seeds and stating the 89.6% +/- 3.6% jackknife SE figure as a conditional ratio of mean contrasts); also stated explicitly that under 6-test Holm adjustment, `U7_true_8s` (p_Holm6=0.00614), `U0_true_8s` (p_Holm6=0.000040), and `U0b_true_8s` (p_Holm6=0.000075) pass alpha=0.05 whereas `U6_true_8s` (p=0.0177, p_Holm6=0.0530) and `U8_true_8s` (p=0.0462, p_Holm6=0.0923) sit marginally above the 6-test Holm threshold; and (3) Reconciled every single per-seed list, sign count, token-class delta, and Table 1C entry in paper_p5.md against experiments_p5/paper5_tables_verified.txt (including I1b, I1c, I1d, U0_s8_linear, U0_true_8s through U8_true_8s, U0_exec_true, U0_s8_extra, C2F_2_pure_filter, C2F_3_outer_gain, C2F_4_gain_form, and all Q1-Q4 entries in Table 1C).",
